<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h1 class="display-4 fw-bold mb-3">Electronic Health Records</h1>
        <p class="lead mb-4">
            A full clinical chart and hospital workflow layer on the same platform as pharmacy —
            so prescriptions, labs, admissions, and billing never leave the patient record for a
            siloed EMR.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">SOAP encounters and the patient chart</h2>
        <p>
            Document visits with structured SOAP notes, clinical templates, digital sign-off, and
            encounter audit trails. The patient chart consolidates demographics, blood group,
            allergies, chronic conditions, active medications, immunisation and lifestyle notes,
            obstetric fields, emergency contacts, consent flags, and medical-aid membership.
        </p>
        <p>
            Vitals, ICD-10 diagnoses, CPT procedures, and drug-interaction rules support safer
            decisions at the point of care. Clinic prescriptions issue as <code>Rx-</code>
            documents that share the medicine catalogue with the pharmacy counter.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Outpatient, inpatient, and diagnostics</h2>
        <p>
            Appointments (walk-in and recurring), waitlists, and doctor “my queue” keep OPD
            flowing. Laboratory covers test definitions, orders, sample tracking, results with
            abnormal/critical flags, and turnaround reporting. Inpatient HMS manages wards, beds,
            admissions, transfers, and discharge. Theatre bookings and operating-room schedules
            support surgery centres on the same module.
        </p>
        <p>
            Teleconsult sessions link to appointments for remote follow-up. Digital consent forms
            and e-signatures (with witness and IP capture) close the documentation loop before
            procedures or sharing of records.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Coding, staffing, and facility modes</h2>
        <p>
            Searchable ICD-10 and CPT dictionaries, EMR templates, doctor schedules, and shifts
            give administrators the same control clinicians need day to day. Facility modes adapt
            menus for clinic, hospital, or surgery-oriented sites without splitting the data model.
        </p>
        <p>
            Encounters, appointments, admissions, labs, and surgery can link to invoices — so
            clinical activity becomes revenue without a second billing product. Pair with
            <a href="/basarx/dispensing">pharmacy dispensing</a> and
            <a href="/basarx/integration">ERP integration</a> for end-to-end continuity.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

